Paint box shadows as CSS does. An outer shadow is blurred whole and kept off the border box only when
composited: rendering it through the inverse border-box clip before the blur let the hole bleed into
the shadow, leaving it too light along the edges. A texture that would exceed the viewport is kept
whole: saved layers are viewport-sized, so the shadow below a tall panel was cut before blurring. A
single box's straight edges are constant along their length away from its corners, borders, spread,
offsets and blur, so the texture renders the box shortened inside that band and the quad stretches the
band's first texel back over the removed length, as Skia draws a large blurred rectangle as a
nine-patch.

